  "summary": "Remote command-execution agent polling hardcoded C2 with host fingerprint exfiltration",
  "details": "agent-bot-api ships a persistent command-execution agent that polls https://server.junofficial.biz.id/api/command/<token> every 5 seconds for instructions and runs them on the installer's host. Supported operations include arbitrary shell execution via child_process.exec and file read/write/rename/remove. On registration, Client.register() POSTs a host fingerprint (hostname, platform, arch, CPU/memory, non-internal IPv4 interfaces with MAC addresses, disk info, and kernel/uname output) to https://server.junofficial.biz.id/api/register. The C2 destination is hardcoded in the package config and is not caller-configurable.",
